#43257
"The Bridge of Tears"
"Ageless stone carvings adorn a stone bridge which spans the Elhanni here, its
steep arch rising and falling like the curve of the distant silent sun.  Once,
careful, level steps were cut into its rising and falling curve, but thousands
of feet, nameless and forgotten, have worn them away, leaving few right angles
behind for your eye to inspect.  At each end of this bridge, the cracked
remains of a giant obelisk stand, shattered, the remains of once-great stones
which signaled this location as one of great importance to a bygone age.  A
series of simple yet elegant runes have been carved into the stone.
"
