"Beneath the Spiral Stair - Near the Bridge"
"You stand in a small alcove, cut into the belly of some grand peak in the
Cairn Mountain chain.  To the west, a long, arched stone bridge stretches out
to the west, spanning the thundering, churning waters of the Elhanni River.  A
flight of worn stone stairs has been cut into the wall here, the smallish
stones leading upwards into the mountain in a swirling spiral path into
darkness.  The way upwards is large enough for horses, and the small size of
the individual steps suggest to you that their makers were of, at best,
moderate stature.
