#43279
"A Secret Altar"
"You are in a rough-hewn cave of great size lit by an other-wordly light that
appears to have no source.  The vaulted ceiling high overhead is unreachable
and throws back whispering echoes of every sound made here.  The walls, rough
though they are, are without large obstructions or sharp rocks, without cracks
or crevices and appear completely solid.  There are only two objects of note
that appear to be permanent fixtures of the cave.  The first is a large stone
altar somewhat north of the caves relative center.  The second is a glowing
black portal like some gaping maw leading into eternal darkness hanging
suspended in the air just in front of the southern-most section of cave wall.
"
